  "HDDS-9447": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-9447",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Implemented",
    "title": "Redundant ACL checks in getKeyInfo for S3 use case",
    "description": "Today, for S3 use case getKeyInfo API needs to look up S3 volume context as the S3 client doesn't know the exact S3 volume. This is done as an optimization that liberates S3 from the need to make an extra call to 'GetS3Volume' per GET key (HDDS-7324).\r\n\r\nRef: [https://github.com/apache/ozone/blob/master/hadoop-ozone/ozone-manager/src/main/java/org/apache/hadoop/ozone/om/OmMetadataReader.java#L160-L169]\r\n\r\nThis getS3VolumeContext contributes to around 30% of getKeyInfo for S3 and creates a performance gap between S3 use case and FSO use case.\r\n\r\nInside getS3VolumeContext, there's an ACL check to validate the client user has access to the S3 volume. This check is redundant because getKeyInfo checks ACL at the key level, which [already covers the volume permission|https://github.com/apache/ozone/blob/master/hadoop-ozone/ozone-manager/src/main/java/org/apache/hadoop/ozone/om/OzoneAclUtils.java#L119].\r\n\r\nThe check dominates the getS3VolumeContext.\r\n\r\n!getS3VolumeContext.png|width=1163,height=519!",
    "commits": [
      {
        "sha": "d17a673cd955207cd36cd972b00c52927482bf33",
        "message": "HDDS-9447. Redundant ACL checks in getKeyInfo for S3 use case",
        "author": "duongkame",
        "date": "2023-10-13T17:15:47Z",
        "files": [
          {
            "PARENT_PATH": "hadoop-ozone/ozone-manager/src/main/java/org/apache/hadoop/ozone/om/OmMetadataReader.java",
            "CHILD_PATH": "hadoop-ozone/ozone-manager/src/main/java/org/apache/hadoop/ozone/om/OmMetadataReader.java",
            "PATH_CHANGED": false,
            "LINES_ADDED": 1,
