  "HDDS-9641": {
    "jira_id": "HDDS-9641",
    "issue_type": "Improvement",
    "resolution": "Fixed",
    "title": "Parallel loading datanode volume db store",
    "description": "Currently the rocksdb that loads schema v3 uses sequential loading and is slow to load, the purpose of this PR is to speed up the loading of the rocksdb using parallel loading.\r\n\r\nThis is my test data:\r\n1. datanode 35 disks * 8TB Wrote about 50% of the capacity\r\n2. after restarting the datanode, it took 5 minutes to load the rocksdb.\r\n\r\n!image-2023-11-07-17-13-29-406.png!\r\n\r\nAfter using this feature:\r\n{code:java}\r\n2023-11-07 16:25:06,699 [main] INFO org.apache.hadoop.ozone.container.ozoneimpl.OzoneContainer: Load 35 volumes DbStore cost: 1532ms {code}\r\n ",
